{"context":"One EKA project groups several repositories (eka-project-understanding: union of registered repos, partitioned by provenance source_repo). Today protocol S3 (runtime/transition.go otherActiveContainer + container.go) enforces exactly-one-active container per PROJECT: a planned container activates only after the active one completes, regardless of repo. For multi-repo projects (e.g. web + mobile) with independent plans, this serializes work that could run in parallel in separate worktrees.","decision":"Allow multiple containers active simultaneously iff (1) SCOPE KEY: each active container's scope is its own source_repo (the repository owning the ctr line; plan's repo does not confer scope); no two active containers share the same source_repo. (2) NO-DEPENDENCY GATE: the transitive closure of the activating container's plan over depends-on/derives-from must share no node with the transitive closure of any other active container's plan (closure over plan lines only, deterministic sorted walk, cycle-safe); a shared node refuses activation naming the shared plan/edge. Same-repo activation keeps the exactly-one-active refusal. Same-plan cross-repo activation refuses via gate (2) (shared plan node). Projections render one board per active container plus a containers summary (multi-active stops being an anomaly warning); eka status stays repo-scoped per ADR-036 with per-repo active shown.","consequences":"If accepted: transitionContainerState activation gate changes from project-wide exactly-one-active to one-active-per-source_repo plus cross-active dependency check; otherActiveContainer becomes scope-aware; view execution/board/containers render one board per active container plus a summary (multi-active stops being an anomaly warning); plan retirement gate and work-item active-container confirmation become scope-aware; /eka-execute Phase 0 can activate per-repo containers in parallel. R10: this decision derives-from req:parallel-container-execution (Discovery intent above); same-stratum depends-on ADR-019/037 documents the amended rules. If rejected: single-active stays; multi-repo teams keep serializing independent work.","alternativesConsidered":"A) Per source_repo only (no dependency check) — simplest, but allows two active containers whose plans depend on each other to diverge. B) Per namespace only — rejected: namespace is identity authority, not execution isolation; one repo can host many namespaces and one project many repos. C) Chosen: per source_repo + no-dependency gate (transitive depends-on/derives-from closure over plan lines between the activating container's plan and every other active container's plan must be disjoint)."}